 "lines": [
  "This diver survived a whale's mouth.",
  "Would you rather get gulped by a whale, or stuck in quicksand?",
  "Pick one right now, and comment A or B. Think fast.",
  "Option [A](eh): the whale. A humpback can grow longer than a school bus.",
  "It feeds by lunging, gulping over five thousand gallons at once.",
  "Cape Cod, [2021](twenty twenty-one). Diver Michael Packard is forty-five feet down.",
  "Suddenly, a huge bump. And everything goes dark.",
  "His first thought: Oh my God, I'm in a whale's mouth.",
  "But a humpback's throat is only about the size of your fist.",
  "Stretched, it's about fifteen inches. You won't fit.",
  "After about thirty seconds, it surfaced and spat him out.",
  "He was badly bruised, but no broken bones.",
  "Option B: quicksand. Sand so soaked with water, it acts like a liquid.",
  "Step on it, and it turns runny. Your legs sink in.",
  "But quicksand is about twice as dense as your body. So you float.",
  "You'd sink to about your waist, and no deeper.",
  "Scientists say yanking a foot out takes the force of lifting a car.",
  "So the real danger is the tide rolling in while you're stuck.",
  "To escape, lean back, spread out, and wiggle your legs slowly.",
  "In [2025](twenty twenty-five), a humpback in Chile gulped a kayaker. Seconds later, he popped up.",
  "By the science, option [A](eh) wins: the whale. Both times, it let go in under a [minute](minnit).",
  "A tiny throat is the reason"
 ],
